Public sources do not settle these points:
- how the official patcher (v1.95, or the newer 2.0 builds bundled inside some patch zips) processes a ._NEW entry;
- whether a new file must also be listed in driveOrder.txt, and in what position;
- what LSN a new file gets in the rebuild, and whether it can go in the root directory;
- whether a rebuild with added files keeps the other files' LSNs;
- how the rebuild treats Cyberbots' directory entries that point at audio tracks.

Settling them would take one of two things, both outside this read-only web task: re-reading the decompiled v1.95 sources (not kept locally; only the EXP-0084 harness Program.cs files remain), or a controlled run of the official core on a Cyberbots copy.

Whether SSP support is still needed, given that egui users cannot apply a patch that adds files, is a user decision.
